## How to Add a New Payment Gateway in the Future

> This section is for Cursor — follow these exact steps when adding any new gateway.
> **Zero changes to existing code** — only additions.

### Step A — Create the Gateway Class

```bash
# Create app/Gateways/PayPalGateway.php (or whichever gateway)
```

```php
<?php

namespace App\Gateways;

use App\Contracts\PaymentGateway;
use App\Models\Order;
use App\Models\PaymentGatewayModel;

class PayPalGateway implements PaymentGateway
{
    private PaymentGatewayModel $gateway;

    public function __construct()
    {
        $this->gateway = PaymentGatewayModel::where('name', 'paypal')->firstOrFail();
        // Initialize PayPal SDK with config from DB
    }

    public function createIntent(Order $order): array
    {
        // PayPal-specific implementation
        return ['orderId' => 'PAYPAL-ORDER-ID'];
    }

    public function verify(string $reference): bool
    {
        // Verify with PayPal API
        return true;
    }

    public function refund(Order $order, float $amount): bool
    {
        // Refund via PayPal API
        return true;
    }
}
```

### Step B — Register in PaymentService

```php
// In app/Services/PaymentService.php — add ONE line to the match():
'paypal' => new PayPalGateway(),
```

### Step C — Add Config Fields in Admin Controller

```php
// In Admin/PaymentGatewayController.php — add to getConfigFields() match():
'paypal' => [
    ['key' => 'client_id',     'label' => 'Client ID',     'type' => 'text',     'filled' => !empty($config['client_id'])],
    ['key' => 'client_secret', 'label' => 'Client Secret', 'type' => 'password', 'filled' => !empty($config['client_secret'])],
],
```

### Step D — Create the Vue Component

```bash
# Create resources/js/Components/Public/Gateways/PayPalPayment.vue
```

### Step E — Register in Checkout Page

```vue
<!-- In Checkout/Index.vue — add one v-else-if block: -->
<PayPalPayment
    v-else-if="selectedGateway === 'paypal'"
    :order-id="order.id"
    :order-total="order.total"
/>
```

### Step F — Add Gateway Icon

```js
// In Checkout/Index.vue and Admin/Settings/Payments.vue — add to gatewayIcons:
paypal: IconBrandPaypal,
```

### Step G — Seed the Gateway

```php
// In a new seeder or directly in tinker:
PaymentGatewayModel::create([
    'name'        => 'paypal',
    'label'       => 'PayPal',
    'description' => 'Pay with your PayPal account.',
    'is_enabled'  => false,  // admin enables it after adding credentials
    'is_test_mode'=> true,
    'sort_order'  => 3,
]);
```

**That's it. 7 small steps. No existing files modified except adding one line to the match() in PaymentService.**

